Intel's Paragon parallel computer (i860 based) runs an OSF/1 based
operating system. At least uname -a says:
    Paragon OSF/1 paragon 1.0.1 T8.0 paragon

As for market penetration - here at the university, we have one - 1 -
Intel Paragon, estimated value $1 500 000, one - 1 - Alpha, estimated
value $15 000, and one - 1 - DECstation 3100 running the development
version of DECs OSF/1, estimated value $3000.

(There was another 3100 running OSF/1, but it was found too buggy
to be usable for that machine.)

Unless DEC gets their act together, they won't be the biggest OSF/1
vendor around here anytime soon.

  - Arne H. Juul



