Starting with the patches available from ftp.ncsa.uiuc.edu in the
DEC_Alpha directory (thanks to Rob McCool!), I made some additional
patches and got a working version of GNU's Bourne Again SHell, bash.
Since this is a very important program (to some people at least :-)
I'm posting my patches here.  Note that you will probably want to
change the default path settings according to your local setup, the
patch to config.h below is very site-dependant.  With these patches,
bash compiles with only some harmless warnings about MAXPATHLEN being
redefined (from 1024 to PATH_MAX, which is also 1024) on our Alpha
running T1.2-2.  Please contact me if you notice any problems with
these patches, but as ususal: Use at own risk, keep unavailable for
children, etc.

Thanks,

   Arne H. Juul, arnej@lise.unit.no

