actually do is pass through control-characters as-is, rather than
converting them to printable form.  Since they are terminal control
sequences generated via termcap, they then make stuff like boldface
characters appear correctly on terminals that support them.

Handy Tip O' The Day:  you can cause less to always display this
behavior by setting the environment variable LESS to be "r".

-Dan


