The DEC product is very close to OSF/1 R1.0.4 as shipped by the OSF.
From what I understand, there are portions of the kernel (VM) that
were modified heavily.  As far as user space (ie what you can see)
is concerned, the DEC command set is at least a superset of 1.0.4 
with the addition of bug fixes.

>	Is DEC's OSF a vendor-specific (dare I say, "proprietary"?)
