This is a strange statement when considering that one of the three
reference platforms for OSF/1 Release 1.0.4 (on which AD is based) is a
MIPS based machine (the DECStation 3100). Now, there may have been a bug...

> If OSF is going to have the "one OS" model of things, then OSF/1 AD
> needs to be either renamed or made the same as OSF/1.  Currently it is
> not the same.

OSF/1 AD lags behind OSF/1 in its development, it is unavoidable. It
takes time to port an integrated kernel to a multicomputer. However, I
don't believe we are trying to obscure the issue. Try doing uname -r (for
release) on your system, it should say 1.0.4.

We are attempting to bring OSF/1 AD up to date wrt the integrated kernel 
and I expect that the next major release of AD will be based on OSF/1 
R1.2 but this will take time and there is a good posibility that OSF/1 
will be on Release 1.3 by then.

