No, no... Methinks there is some confusion here.  If your /etc/motd has
"DEC OSF/1 V1.2 (Rev. 10)", you have the official release of DEC OSF/1 V1.2
on Alpha AXP.  Many people who field tested V1.2 refer to this version as
"BL12" (for "baselevel 12").  The second external field test release, which
was "BL10", had an motd of "DEC OSF/1 T1.2-2 (Rev. ??)" (there was a real
Rev. number there, which I don't remember what it was, but I think it was
somewhere between 40 and 60).

Another way to tell is to run "file /vmunix".  The compiler in the official
release of V1.2 stamps its executables with "version 3.11", while the compiler
in the second external field test stamps its executables with "version 10.0".

Hope this helps...

