   I've administered a DEC 3000/500 Alpha workstation for at least 9 months, both
   under OpenVMS and OSF/1.  DEC's OSF/1 is fine.  Only a few minor differences
n   from other flavors of unix.  Usenet software ports easily.  Damn fast X
   windows!!!  As far as that goes, a damned fast system.

   The only real complaint I have is that DEC doesn't support OS upgrades.  To
   upgrade the OS, you actually have to reinstall and reconfigure from scratch
   (just like SunOS).  Sure makes it hard to customize and localize a system when
   you have to do it over and over with every new release.

 
	I don't like the reinstall either, but remember that until
this last release your were running field test stuff. DEC has gotten
the concept of upgrades with ULTRIX, so I would expect them to do the
same with OSF/1 now that we are running an official commercial
release.


